---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import diagram from '../../styles/components/diagram.css?url';
import film from '../../styles/components/film.css?url';
import marquee from '../../styles/components/marquee.css?url';
import page from '../../styles/projects/breathment.css?url';
---

<ProjectLayout slug="breathment" styles={[diagram, film, marquee, page]}>
  <div class="cover">
    <figure class="cv-img">
      <img
        src="/media/breathment/cover.webp"
        alt="The Breathment website on a desktop screen, with paths for COPD, asthma and lung cancer, beside the app’s My Day and Progress screens on two phones"
      />
    </figure>
    <div class="cv-deco" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="cv-ring"></span>
      <svg class="cv-ln" viewBox="0 0 106 30">
        <polyline class="cl" points="4.3,1.2 105.4,29.5"></polyline>
      </svg>
      <span class="x cv-x1"></span>
      <span class="x cv-x2"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="sec first" id="s-overview" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-overview">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-overview">
        Overview
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split-a">
        <p class="lead">From the patient app to internal tools.</p>
        <p class="tx">
          Breathment advances digital therapies for people with chronic respiratory conditions using AI-supported health
          solutions. I joined as UI/UX Designer and worked across the full product, from the patient-facing app to
          internal admin tools and communication systems.
        </p>
        <p class="tx">
          As the only designer on the team, I worked on both the website and the app, and took on other roles along the
          way, from graphic design to marketing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-b">
        <span class="vl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <dl class="facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Status</dt>
            <dd>Delivered</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Tools</dt>
            <dd>Figma, ProtoPie, Illustrator, After Effects, Blender</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Live</dt>
            <dd>
              <a class="ul" href="https://breathment.com/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                Visit breathment.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="roles rv"
      role="group"
      aria-label="One designer across three areas: product, with the patient app, the website and internal tools; visuals, with illustrations and the character; and communication, with graphic design and marketing"
    >
      <div class="ro-top">
        <span class="mk navy" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <b>Sole designer</b>
        <small>one person across the whole product</small>
      </div>
      <div class="ro-bus" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="hd"></span>
        <span class="ro-bc"></span>
        <span class="ro-bc up"></span>
        <span class="ro-bc"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="ro-g">
        <span class="mk navy" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="ulabel">Product</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Patient app</li>
          <li>Website</li>
          <li>Admin tools and communication systems</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ro-g">
        <span class="mk mint" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="ulabel">Visuals</span>
        <ul>
          <li>24 illustrations</li>
          <li>Character and expressions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ro-g">
        <span class="mk ring" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="ulabel">Communication</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Graphic design</li>
          <li>Marketing</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="s-app" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-app">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-app">
        Patient app
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="lead">Daily exercises, courses and progress in one app.</p>
      <p class="tx">
        My Day opens with what is due today: the weekly health check, the exercises waiting and any left from yesterday.
        Explore gathers short courses, from an introduction to COPD to travel, everyday life and nutrition, and Progress
        shows the week at a glance.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="mock rv">
      <img
        src="/media/breathment/app-screens.webp"
        alt="Three app screens: Courses with Introduction to COPD, Travel, COPD in Everyday and Nutrition; My Day with the weekly health check, available exercises and yesterday’s exercises; and Progress with the week’s calendar"
        style="aspect-ratio: 2656 / 2231"
      />
      <figcaption>Explore, My Day and Progress</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="notes3">
      <div class="rv">
        <h4>My Day</h4>
        <p>The weekly health check, today’s exercises and yesterday’s leftovers, each one tap from starting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rv">
        <h4>Explore</h4>
        <p>Short courses on living with COPD, from the basics to travel, everyday life and nutrition.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rv">
        <h4>Progress</h4>
        <p>A week view with exercises waiting and done, so the routine stays visible.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="split" style="margin-top: 72px; align-items: center">
      <div class="split-a">
        <span class="ulabel">Progress, in context</span>
        <p class="lead">More than a count of exercises.</p>
        <p class="tx">
          Alongside the exercises, Progress shows the air quality outside, daily steps against a goal, the days left in
          a programme, active days and a streak, so each day’s activity has context.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="rv" style="margin: 0">
        <img
          class="pg"
          src="/media/breathment/progress-screens.webp"
          alt="Two Progress screens: the week view with today’s exercises and air quality, and cards for activity steps, programme progress, active days and streak"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="s-diary" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-diary">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-diary">
        Diary
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="lead">Health tracking that older users can keep up with.</p>
      <p class="tx">
        Older users need a simple way to monitor health measurements, understand changes over time and keep a consistent
        tracking routine. Traditional health dashboards are hard to navigate, with complex medical data, dense
        interfaces and too many options.
      </p>
      <p class="tx">
        The diary is built around simplicity, accessibility and clear data visualisation. Users pick the metrics that
        matter to them, enter new measurements quickly, follow their progress in easy-to-read charts, complete periodic
        health checks and set personal reminders.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="scr3">
      <figure class="rv">
        <img
          src="/media/breathment/diary-home.webp"
          alt="Diary home with measurements and the weekly health check"
          style="aspect-ratio: 142 / 302"
        />
        <figcaption class="ulabel">Diary home</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="rv">
        <img
          src="/media/breathment/peak-flow-chart.webp"
          alt="Peak flow rate chart by week, month and year"
          style="aspect-ratio: 142 / 301"
        />
        <figcaption class="ulabel">Peak flow</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="rv">
        <img
          src="/media/breathment/measurements-list.webp"
          alt="Measurements list with today’s values and personal metrics"
          style="aspect-ratio: 142 / 301"
        />
        <figcaption class="ulabel">Measurements</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="notes3">
      <div class="rv">
        <h4>Progressive disclosure</h4>
        <p>Details appear only when they are needed, which keeps each screen light.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rv">
        <h4>Focused actions</h4>
        <p>Consistent navigation and focused actions make everyday entries quick.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rv">
        <h4>Customisable content</h4>
        <p>Users choose the metrics and reminders that matter to them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tags-row">
      <ul class="tg" aria-label="Methods">
        <li>Information architecture</li>
        <li>Wireframes</li>
        <li>Prototyping</li>
      </ul>
      <a
        class="cta ul lift"
        href="https://www.figma.com/proto/7TCbbzH8zfnjbeXvU3DHeM/Portfolio?node-id=29-9218&amp;t=qqoqRJZFLmaJii9u-0&amp;scaling=min-zoom&amp;content-scaling=fixed&amp;page-id=29%3A8082&amp;hide-ui=1"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        View prototype <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="s-website" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-website">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-website">
        Website
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="lead">A website that starts from the condition.</p>
      <p class="tx">
        The homepage opens with three paths, one each for COPD, asthma and lung cancer, so patients can find their own
        way in, while solutions, providers, pricing and a demo booking stay one click away. Designing the website and
        the app together kept one visual language from the first visit to daily use.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="mock rv">
      <img
        src="/media/breathment/website-homepage.webp"
        alt="Breathment homepage with three image panels: I have COPD, I have Asthma and I have Lung Cancer, each with a See more link"
        style="aspect-ratio: 1016 / 634"
      />
      <figcaption>Homepage, with one path per condition</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="s-illustrations" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-illustrations">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-illustrations">
        Illustrations
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="lead">24 scenes that make respiratory care feel human.</p>
      <p class="tx">
        A series of custom illustrations in one consistent visual language, tailored to the Breathment app. Each scene
        makes a complex respiratory health topic more approachable, from asthma basics to inhaler technique and daily
        management.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="band" role="group" aria-label="All 24 illustrations, sliding">
      <div class="track">
        <img
          src="/media/breathment/illustrations-grid.webp"
          alt="Grid of 24 Breathment illustrations, from types of asthma medications to asthma and infections"
        />
        <img src="/media/breathment/illustrations-grid.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
        <img src="/media/breathment/illustrations-grid.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
        <img src="/media/breathment/illustrations-grid.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cap">Figma and Adobe Illustrator · Hover to pause</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="s-character" data-sec aria-labelledby="h-character">
    <div class="sh">
      <h2 class="sh-t" id="h-character">
        Character
      </h2>
      <span class="sh-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="x sh-x" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="lead">A companion that lives across the app.</p>
      <p class="tx">
        The character is closely aligned with the app’s content concept. It strengthens engagement as a visual and
        interactive element, with expressive features and one design language across illustrations, UI components and
        communication materials.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="chars">
      <figure class="rv">
        <img
          class="ch-main"
          src="/media/breathment/character-main.webp"
          alt="Main Breathment character, a soft mint and blue cloud with big eyes"
          style="aspect-ratio: 307 / 323"
        />
        <figcaption class="ulabel">Main character · Illustrator and Figma</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="rv">
        <img
          src="/media/breathment/character-variations.webp"
          alt="Four variations of the character with different expressions"
          style="aspect-ratio: 242 / 323"
        />
        <figcaption class="ulabel">Expressions</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
